---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_URL, SITE_TITLE, X_HANDLE, X_URL } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Who runs nano-api, how it is built, and what that means for you as a customer."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="page">
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<h1>One person, small tools, no roadmap theatre.</h1>

				<p>
					nano-api is a family of single-purpose APIs. Each one lives on its own subdomain, takes
					one API key, and does a job you would otherwise run a server for.
				</p>

				<h2>How it is built</h2>
				<p>
					Cloudflare Workers at the edge, D1 for storage, a scheduled trigger for the background
					work. No servers, no containers, no queue to babysit — which is why the free tier can
					exist at all.
				</p>
				<p>
					API keys are stored as SHA-256 hashes, never in clear text. Rotate and revoke them
					yourself, without asking me.
				</p>

				<h2>What to expect</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Answers from the person who wrote the code, usually the same day.</li>
					<li>Honest limits: if something is not built, the page says so.</li>
					<li>No dark patterns, and no "contact sales" wall in front of the numbers.</li>
					<li>Delete a monitor and it is gone, history included.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>What not to expect</h2>
				<p>
					An enterprise SLA, phone support, or nine nines. Where a missed alert has serious
					consequences, run two providers — I would tell a friend the same thing.
				</p>

				<h2>Get in touch</h2>
				<p>
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or
					<a href={X_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{X_HANDLE}</a> on X. Code on
					<a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.page {
		max-width: 44em;
		padding: 2em 0 0;
	}
	.page h2 {
		margin-top: 2em;
		font-size: 1.4rem;
	}
	.page p,
	.page li {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.page ul {
		padding-left: 1.2em;
	}
	.page li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
</style>
